  "query_preview": "..\nDry conditions continue for all the Marianas with the exception of \nisland effect showers possible for all islands Tuesday, as winds \ncontinue to weaken. These will likely remain shallow and short lived \nin nature due to dry air in the upper levels of the atmosphere. By \nFriday night, rainbands ahead of Invest 96W, currently still north of\nKosrae, may begin to move into the region and bring scattered \nshowers and some thunderstorms. By Saturday, heavy showers are \nlikely, becoming widespread heavy showers that night as 96W passes \nnear or through the Marianas. Heavy showers will likely continue \nthrough Sunday and possibly Sunday night before conditions start to \nclear out Monday. Gusty winds are expected to begin Saturday as well \nand last through Sunday night. The track and intensity of 96W remains\nhighly uncertain as the system has yet to organize and is still 5 to\n6 days out. Residents in the Marianas should continue to monitor \nforecasts over the next several days, and maintain a general state of\npreparedness in case of a potential tropical storm or typhoon. See \nthe \"Tropical Systems\" section for more details on 96W.",
